OpenFig
--------

OpenFig is an independent personal fork of
https://github.com/aws/amazon-q-developer-cli-autocomplete (originally Fig).
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Amazon, AWS, Fig or terminal vendors.
Names and integration icons identify their respective products; no trademark
rights are granted by this repository's software licenses.

The upstream MIT / Apache-2.0 license texts and copyright notice are retained.
For distribution of the upstream dual-licensed project code, this fork uses
the MIT option. OpenFig contributions are also offered under MIT OR Apache-2.0.
This does not relicense components that have their own terms.

OpenFig changes include removing product AI/chat, sign-in, telemetry and
automatic updates; bundling completion specs; replacing PTY interception with
zsh integration; and adding bounded native workers and input-method recovery.
Completion generators can execute user commands, including network commands.

Vendored components:
- specs/: withfig/autocomplete, MIT; see specs/LICENSE.
- packages/spec-types/, spec-generators/, spec-helpers/, spec-compiler/:
  withfig/autocomplete-tools, MIT; each directory retains LICENSE.
- packages/fuzzysort/: farzher/fuzzysort, MIT; LICENSE retains Stephen Kamenar's
  copyright. The package wrapper and integration have been modified.
- crates/macos-utils/accessibility-master/: eiz/accessibility, MIT OR Apache-2.0;
  LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE retain the upstream terms and copyright.
  OpenFig modifies ownership, thread confinement, errors and query budgets.
  License source: eiz/accessibility revision 173e898d4a52ee0afe0224ecb458d324057856e7.

Locked dependency versions, source locations, copyright and license texts are
listed in packages/dashboard-app/public/license/NOTICE.txt and included in
built apps. Regenerate that file with scripts/license-notices.py when updating
dependencies. It includes build/test tools as well as runtime dependencies.

The application's replacement icon is generated by bundle/macos/icon-gen/.
Unlicensed external theme payloads are not distributed. Only the source's
built-in dark, light and system themes are supplied by default. Custom local
themes require separate redistribution review.
